Description: IMAP and SMTP via MCP Server
 mcp-email-server is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that lets
 MCP-compatible AI clients read, search, organize, and send email over
 IMAP and SMTP. Accounts and credentials are configured via environment
 variables or a local managed store; the server is invoked over stdio
 (mcp-server-email stdio) or as an HTTP/SSE transport.

Package: mcprack-mcp-server-email
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 mcprack (>= 1.5.1),
 mcp-server-email (= ${binary:Version}),
Description: Registers Email MCP server into mcprack catalog
 Companion package for mcp-server-email. Installing it registers the
 mcp-server-email binary (stdio transport) as an available MCP server
 in the local mcprack instance; removing it unregisters it again.
